1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,950
Tonight, tiny pieces of Halley's Comet are slamming into Earth.
今晚，哈雷彗星的碎片正在砸向地球。

2
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:05,690
At 66 kilometers per second.
速度是每秒66公里。

3
00:00:05,690 --> 00:00:07,760
That's about 150,000 miles an hour.
差不多每小时24万公里。

4
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:10,250
And you can watch it from your backyard.
而你在自家后院就能看。

5
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:11,860
It's the Orionid meteor shower,
这就是猎户座流星雨，

6
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:13,220
peaking right about now.
差不多正在极大期。

7
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:16,320
Today's question: how does a speck smaller than a grain of sand
今天的问题：一粒比沙子还小的灰，

8
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:17,570
light up the whole sky?
怎么能把整片天空点亮？

9
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:18,220
Meet Dusty.
认识一下小尘。

10
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:20,440
Dusty is a crumb of Halley's Comet.
小尘是哈雷彗星掉下来的一点渣。

11
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:22,490
Halley's Comet swings by the Sun
哈雷彗星大约每76年

12
00:00:22,490 --> 00:00:23,950
about every 76 years.
绕太阳回来一次。

13
00:00:23,950 --> 00:00:25,470
Each time, the Sun cooks it,
每次靠近，太阳一烤，

14
00:00:25,470 --> 00:00:27,700
and it sheds dust like a dog sheds fur.
它就掉灰，像狗掉毛。

15
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,020
Over thousands of orbits,
绕了几千圈，

16
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:31,350
that dust spreads into a long, dirty ring.
这些灰铺成了一条长长的脏带子。

17
00:00:31,350 --> 00:00:33,780
Every October, Earth drives right through it.
每年十月，地球正好从里面穿过。

18
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:35,090
Same time, every year.
年年同一时间。

19
00:00:35,090 --> 00:00:36,840
Like driving through a cloud of bugs
就像在高速公路上

20
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:37,680
on the highway.
开进一团飞虫。

21
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:39,250
Twist one: we hit it head-on.
反转一：我们是迎头撞上的。

22
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:41,810
Halley orbits the Sun the opposite way to us.
哈雷彗星绕太阳的方向跟地球相反。

23
00:00:41,810 --> 00:00:42,930
So the speeds add up.
所以速度要相加。

24
00:00:42,930 --> 00:00:45,080
Head-on collisions are the worst kind.
迎面相撞，最狠。

25
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:46,630
66 kilometers per second
每秒66公里，

26
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:49,780
is roughly 70 times faster than a rifle bullet.
大约是步枪子弹的70倍。

27
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:51,670
And energy grows with speed squared.
而能量跟速度的平方走。

28
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:53,830
Double the speed, four times the punch.
速度翻倍，冲击翻四倍。

29
00:00:53,830 --> 00:00:56,960
Our rough estimate: a one-milligram speck at that speed
我们估算一下：1毫克的小灰，这个速度，

30
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:58,620
carries about 2,000 joules.
带着大约两千焦耳的能量。

31
00:00:58,620 --> 00:00:59,540
That's more energy
这比一颗手枪子弹的能量

32
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:00,730
than a pistol bullet.
还要大。

33
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:02,180
Twist two: it's not friction
反转二：让它发光的，

34
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:03,280
that makes it glow.
不是摩擦。

35
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:05,830
Dusty is so fast, the air can't get out of the way.
小尘太快了，空气来不及让开，

36
00:01:05,830 --> 00:01:08,390
It piles up in front, squeezed and scorching hot.
在它前面挤成一堆，又烫又密。

37
00:01:08,390 --> 00:01:10,430
Squeeze air hard enough and fast enough,
空气被挤得又狠又快，

38
00:01:10,430 --> 00:01:12,440
and it heats to thousands of degrees.
就能热到几千度。

39
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:14,000
Like a bike pump getting hot,
就像打气筒会发烫，

40
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,190
but on fast-forward.
只不过开了快进。

41
00:01:15,190 --> 00:01:17,040
Dusty boils away, atom by atom,
小尘一个原子一个原子地蒸发掉，

42
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:18,840
more than 100 kilometers up.
大约在一百多公里的高空。

43
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:21,480
Those hot atoms, and the air around them, glow.
这些滚烫的原子和周围的空气在发光，

44
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:22,550
Like a neon sign.
就像霓虹灯。

45
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:24,980
So the streak you see is not a rock on fire.
所以你看到的那道光，不是一块烧着的石头，

46
00:01:24,980 --> 00:01:27,520
It's a tube of glowing air, kilometers long.
而是一条几公里长、发光的空气管子。

47
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:28,870
Twist three, the weird part:
反转三，最反直觉：

48
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:30,720
the streak is way bigger than Dusty.
那道光比小尘大太多了。

49
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:32,870
A crumb you could lose on your fingertip
放在指尖上都找不到的一点渣，

50
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:35,670
makes a line you can see from 100 kilometers away.
能划出一百公里外都看得见的线。

51
00:01:35,670 --> 00:01:38,240
About half the Orionids even leave glowing trails
大约一半的猎户座流星，还会留下发光的尾迹，

52
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:40,140
that hang in the sky for a moment.
在天上停一会儿。

53
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:41,890
And none of them reach the ground.
而且它们一个都落不到地上。

54
00:01:41,890 --> 00:01:44,060
Dusty is gone long before it gets close.
没到半路，小尘就没了。

55
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:46,660
How to watch: go out in the dark hours before dawn
怎么看：天亮前那几个小时，

56
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:48,340
and get away from city lights.
离城市的灯光远一点。

57
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:49,920
The Moon sets around 2 a.m.,
月亮大约凌晨两点落下，

58
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,960
so the sky gets darker after that.
之后天更黑。

59
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:53,300
Look anywhere in the sky.
看天上哪里都行。

60
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:55,630
The streaks all seem to fly out of Orion.
流星都像是从猎户座里飞出来的。

61
00:01:55,630 --> 00:01:57,010
Give your eyes 20 minutes.
给眼睛20分钟适应。

62
00:01:57,010 --> 00:01:58,410
And put your phone away.
还有，把手机收起来。

63
00:01:58,410 --> 00:02:01,340
Friendly fine print: maybe 15 to 20 an hour at best,
友情提示：最好的时候，一小时也就15到20颗，

64
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:03,260
so bring patience and a blanket.
带上耐心和一条毯子。

65
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:06,380
Missed it? Halley's dust comes back every October.
错过了？哈雷的灰每年十月都会回来。

66
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:08,630
And Halley itself returns in 2061.
哈雷彗星本尊，2061年回来。

67
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:11,340
Dusty waited thousands of years for this moment.
小尘等了几千年，就为这一刻。

68
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:14,060
It lasted one second, and it was glorious.
只亮了一秒，可是真灿烂。

